-- title:
--   Surjective trace ML(H_Q)toML(H_R) with augmentation kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative local ring with residue field $k$, let $p$ and $N\ge 1$ be natural numbers, $S$ a set of natural numbers, $r\ge 4$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to $k$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t\ge 1$, let $\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_t\in k$, and for each $i$ let $\pi^\Delta_i\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ be a homomorphism. Put $L=N(\prod_i q_i)r$, $H_R=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/r)^\times\big)$ and $H_Q=H_R\cap\ker\pi_Q$, where $\pi_Q$ is assembled from the $\pi^\Delta_i$. For $H\in\{H_Q,H_R\}$ the carrier is $H^1$ of level $L$ and character group $H$ with coefficients $\mathcal O$, equipped with operators $\mathrm{op}(g)$ indexed by the generators $g$ of type $\mathrm{Gen}(L,S,t)$, namely symbols $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and symbols $U_i$ for $i\in\{1,\dots,t\}$; $\mathrm{ML}$ denotes the localisation of this carrier at the complement of the prime ideal $\mathfrak m_\theta=\ker(\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \mathrm{Gen}(L,S,t)\ \mathcal O\to k)$, the map sending $X_{T_\ell}\mapsto\theta(T_\ell)$ and $X_{U_i}\mapsto\alpha_i$, so that $\mathrm{ML}$ is a module over $\mathcal O$ and over the free algebra. Assume the operators $\mathrm{op}(g)$ commute pairwise on the carrier for $H_Q$ (hypothesis `hcQ`) and for $H_R$ (hypothesis `hcR`), and that for $H_Q$ every diamond operator $\langle u\rangle$, $u\in(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$, commutes with every $\mathrm{op}(g)$ (hypothesis `hdc`), whence each $\langle u\rangle$ induces an $\mathcal O$-linear endomorphism $\mathrm{diaML}(u)$ of $\mathrm{ML}(H_Q)$. Then there exists an $\mathcal O$-linear map $\lambda_0\colon\mathrm{ML}(H_Q)\to\mathrm{ML}(H_R)$ which is surjective, satisfies $\lambda_0(X_g\cdot x)=X_g\cdot\lambda_0(x)$ for every generator $g$ and every $x$, satisfies $\lambda_0(\mathrm{diaML}(u)x)=\lambda_0(x)$ for all $u\in H_R$ and all $x$, and has $\lambda_0(x)=0$ exactly when $x$ lies in the $\mathcal O$-submodule spanned by the elements $\mathrm{diaML}(u)z-z$ with $u\in H_R$ and $z\in\mathrm{ML}(H_Q)$.
--
--   This is the Taylor–Wiles covering step at auxiliary level: the localised corestriction (transfer) along the finite-index normal inclusion $\Gamma_{H_Q}(L)\le\Gamma_{H_R}(L)$ is onto, commutes with the Hecke symbols, is invariant under the diamond operators coming from $H_R$, and its kernel is the augmentation submodule generated by the $\langle u\rangle z-z$. It is used in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_monoidAlgebra_and_basis_ML_HQ`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_monoidAlgebra_and_basis_ML_HQ) and in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_basis_ML_monoidAlgebra_and_linearMap_ML_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_basis_ML_monoidAlgebra_and_linearMap_ML_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq), where $\mathrm{ML}(H_Q)$ is exhibited as a free module over the group algebra of $H_R/H_Q$ with quotient $\mathrm{ML}(H_R)$.
